      "Content strategy: publish for the audience, not the affiliate link\nThe source describes a demanding publishing rhythm—roughly two or three videos per day over an extended period. Treat that as an example of the consistency required, not a universal algorithm rule or guaranteed posting formula.",
      "A practical content mix could include:\n- Useful explainers: answer common questions in the niche.\n- Comparisons: explain differences between product types or approaches.\n- Demonstrations: show how a product category is used, where truthful and properly represented.\n- Opinion and perspective: give the character a recognisable point of view without inventing personal experiences.\n- Audience questions: respond to recurring questions and confusion.\n- Relevant recommendations: introduce products only when they fit the subject and audience need.\nDo not make every post a sales pitch. If the only reason to follow the page is to see the next affiliate link, there is little reason to stay.\nA repeatable AI-assisted content workflow\nStep 1: Select one audience question.\nStart with a real question, recurring problem, or useful topic—not simply “What can I post today?”",
