      "This is the model ranked first in the source because the cost of delivering another copy is close to zero.\nWhy digital products have attractive economics\nA physical product must be manufactured, stored, packed, and shipped each time. A digital product is created once and can be delivered repeatedly at very low marginal cost.",
      "That does not mean the business has no costs. You still have:\n- Research and production time.\n- AI and design subscriptions.\n- Payment-processing fees.\n- Platform or hosting costs.\n- Customer acquisition.\n- Customer support.\n- Refunds and chargebacks.\n- Updates and maintenance.\n- Taxes and business administration.\nBut the marginal delivery cost of the next copy is usually much lower than the cost of shipping another physical item.\nThe most important principle: build for an audience, not in isolation\nThe source's strongest example is a creator who teaches video editing and sells editing guides to people who already watch that content.",
